possible that the user changed an existing script to abstract after it was attached to a node. When this happens, the user needs to fix it, and we should keep track of the global class name to allow the \"Extend Script\" button to work.\r\n\r\nIn master: The \"Extend Script...\" button is hidden, and an unhelpful error message is printed. It is still possible for users to workaround the issue by \"Change Type...\" to a class extending the abstract class, or dragging a script into the inspector.\r\n\r\nIn this PR: The \"Extend Script...\" button appears, auto-fills with the class name, and a helpful error message is printed.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1220\" height=\"681\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-23 at 2 39 00 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8e246355-e641-4c2f-8eee-6bf718ec04f1\" />\r\n\r\nThis PR still isn't perfect, for example we should have some way of marking the loaded scene as changed even though the user has made no changes, but I don't know if the PackedScene class has this capability. I'm open to suggestions.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518733,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg3MzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/usability","name":"usability","description":"","color":"447744","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/g